1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Honestly, I don't think your band
can go on like this.

2
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:11,320
<i>What about that great guy you said</i>
<i>you want in the band? What did he say?</i>

3
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:14,240
<i>This time, he'll definitely say yes.</i>

4
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:17,120
<i>You've cut yourself off</i>
<i>from the outside world so much,</i>

5
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:19,040
<i>you don't know what's going on out there.</i>

6
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:21,640
<i>It's just one clip,</i>
<i>but it has millions of views.</i>

7
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:24,880
<i>Someone came to audition.</i>
<i>He said his name was Phatee.</i>

8
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,000
I found your band's selling point.

9
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:30,720
<i>I agree to become a trainee</i>

10
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:32,119
<i>and debut with your band.</i>

11
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:34,160
<i>Thanks for doing this for our dream.</i>

12
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:35,920
<i>Our band gets to keep going!</i>

13
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:43,560
P-ONE MUSIC LABEL - ARTIST CONTRACT

14
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:52,080
Artist contract.

15
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:55,960
According to the contract,
the label's trainees

16
00:00:56,520 --> 00:00:58,280
can't take other jobs.

17
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:00,360
Are you okay with that?

18
00:01:05,519 --> 00:01:07,000
Do whatever you want.

19
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:09,720
I've never stopped you.

20
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:12,280
Besides,

21
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:14,760
you don't like taking jobs
at the club anyway.

22
00:01:15,640 --> 00:01:17,640
Actually, becoming an artist is good too.

23
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:21,480
If you become famous, I'll print
your photo and put it up at the club,

24
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:23,040
and tell everyone that I

25
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:24,640
made you a star.

26
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:29,560
Thank you.

27
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:31,960
Then I'll hurry and move my stuff out.

28
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,360
Why are you moving your stuff?

29
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:36,360
Is your label making you live there?

30
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:39,360
I don't work for you anymore.

31
00:01:39,440 --> 00:01:41,480
Do I still have the right to use the room?

32
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:46,280
You know, becoming an artist takes time.

33
00:01:46,360 --> 00:01:48,400
To release a song,

34
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:50,600
to get famous, to build a fanbase,

35
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:52,360
it takes time.

36
00:01:55,360 --> 00:01:56,840
You don't have to move out.

37
00:01:56,920 --> 00:01:57,840
Stay here.

38
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:17,640
You're not staying for free.

39
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:20,440
I'll definitely charge you rent.

40
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:22,200
I just haven't figured out yet

41
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:24,240
how much to charge you.

42
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:44,720
Enough.

43
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:47,040
Enough.

44
00:02:50,280 --> 00:02:51,120
Thank you.

45
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:55,640
Then I'll go practice.

46
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:11,040
He's only a trainee,
and you're already this happy.

47
00:03:11,120 --> 00:03:12,760
If he becomes an artist,

48
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:15,440
won't you throw a three-day party
for the whole block?

49
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:18,640
Well, I'm proud of him.

50
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:20,320
Who would've thought

51
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:22,480
a broken-winged crow like Phatee

52
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:24,680
would actually get to
follow his real dream?

53
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:29,040
When I went to Japan,
you weren't this proud of me.

54
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:30,520
Vann!

55
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:35,120
Hey, Japan boy.

56
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:36,520
You totally disappeared.

57
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:38,160
I've been studying hard.

58
00:03:38,240 --> 00:03:39,400
Studying hard?

59
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:41,680
If you're studying hard,
how come you're here?

60
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:42,720
Can I get another one?

61
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:45,280
I really missed your nagging
when I was in Japan.

62
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:46,200
Stop.

63
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:48,400
I'm not playing along.

64
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,640
What? I didn't skip class.

65
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:54,600
If you don't believe me, ask Rakkhun.

66
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:55,800
Right, darling?

67
00:03:58,480 --> 00:04:01,160
It's a long holiday in Japan right now.

68
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:02,800
So I booked him a ticket back.

69
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:05,080
See?

70
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:07,680
You two are really in sync.

71
00:04:09,720 --> 00:04:11,520
Whatever. I've given up.

72
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:13,800
No matter what rules I make,

73
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:17,440
none of the crows around here follow them.

74
00:04:18,440 --> 00:04:19,880
Just look at Talay.

75
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:23,160
He's even seeing that writer guy.

76
00:04:24,280 --> 00:04:25,840
Hey, you.

77
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:27,640
Why are you coming at me?

78
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:29,920
It's just a temporary relationship.

79
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,280
I'm not serious about it.

80
00:04:32,080 --> 00:04:33,560
Whatever.

81
00:04:34,960 --> 00:04:36,480
Every crow here

82
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:38,160
is stubborn.

83
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:45,360
<i>Is this yours?</i>

84
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:48,600
SUN: IS THIS YOURS?

85
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:52,320
You and that writer…

86
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:54,160
Did it happen?

87
00:04:54,760 --> 00:04:55,560
What's with you?

88
00:04:55,640 --> 00:04:57,160
Stay out of it.

89
00:04:57,240 --> 00:04:59,040
Don't worry about me.

90
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:02,320
And bring me a souvenir.

91
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:07,320
Linda.

92
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:08,560
Your souvenir.

93
00:05:10,360 --> 00:05:11,880
I'm charging you.

94
00:06:37,320 --> 00:06:39,760
I didn't think someone like
you would bring me here.

95
00:06:43,040 --> 00:06:45,480
You wanted to know more about
who I am, didn't you?

96
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:47,560
What someone like me does all day.

97
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:50,880
So you can use it
as material for your novel.

98
00:07:08,320 --> 00:07:10,720
Did you really draw these yourself?

99
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:12,840
You're not pretending to be
an artist to fool me, are you?

100
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:20,720
Want to try drawing one?

101
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:23,480
I'm not good at drawing.

102
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:34,480
Every drawing is beautiful.

103
00:07:35,360 --> 00:07:37,040
It depends on how you see it.

104
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:44,600
If you don't want to draw,

105
00:07:46,320 --> 00:07:47,920
why don't you try writing something?

106
00:07:48,920 --> 00:07:50,240
You're a writer, aren't you?

107
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:27,040
Virginia Woolf.

108
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:48,520
Then draw me.

109
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:51,200
No.

110
00:08:53,360 --> 00:08:54,880
I don't draw people.

111
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:59,400
Why? Afraid it won't look good?

112
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:01,680
With your brushwork,

113
00:09:01,760 --> 00:09:03,960
I think you could paint a cool portrait.

114
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:06,440
I don't want to.

115
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:10,040
What makes you think you can judge
what's good or bad about me?

116
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:12,320
I told you, you don't know me well.

117
00:09:13,120 --> 00:09:14,280
You see my face

118
00:09:14,360 --> 00:09:16,600
and judge me by my appearance
like everyone else.

119
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:22,160
Last night,
I saw more than just your face.

120
00:09:32,520 --> 00:09:34,120
Did you leave anything else in my room?

121
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:49,480
Next time, I definitely won't forget.

122
00:09:57,800 --> 00:09:59,560
There'll be a next time, right?

123
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:04,360
Let me see how today goes first.

124
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:22,400
Everyone,

125
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:24,240
come here.

126
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:30,120
Let's officially
introduce ourselves again.

127
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:31,680
This is Phatee.

128
00:10:32,360 --> 00:10:34,920
He'll be the main vocalist of A-team.

129
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:39,080
And I have more good news for you.

130
00:10:39,160 --> 00:10:41,440
Your debut

131
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:43,040
is in three months.

132
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:51,880
Just do your best.

133
00:10:51,960 --> 00:10:54,320
And take care of Phatee.

134
00:10:55,120 --> 00:10:56,520
You can count on us.

135
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:02,880
Finally! Guys,

136
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:04,640
we're finally debuting!

137
00:11:05,400 --> 00:11:06,600
Hi.

138
00:11:06,680 --> 00:11:07,720
I'm PJ.

139
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:10,160
I'm the keyboardist for A-team.

140
00:11:10,240 --> 00:11:11,520
Welcome.

141
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:14,320
Okay.

142
00:11:16,560 --> 00:11:18,480
Hi. I'm Tonhon.

143
00:11:18,560 --> 00:11:20,440
I'm the bassist.

144
00:11:20,520 --> 00:11:21,680
And

145
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:24,320
with a face this handsome, I'm the visual.

146
00:11:27,080 --> 00:11:28,360
Okay.

147
00:11:28,440 --> 00:11:30,200
Saw. I'm the drummer.

148
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:35,520
Saw also produces.

149
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:36,800
He can write songs.

150
00:11:36,880 --> 00:11:38,280
He can play guitar.

151
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:39,440
You guys should hit it off.

152
00:11:43,680 --> 00:11:46,400
So, aren't you going to
introduce yourself, big bro?

153
00:11:46,480 --> 00:11:48,560
How do you know I'm older?

154
00:11:48,640 --> 00:11:50,120
I could be younger than you.

155
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,920
Kao told me you're the oldest in the band.

156
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:57,480
So I figured you'd be older than me.

157
00:12:00,080 --> 00:12:01,080
That stings.

158
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:02,840
Hey, man. Don't let it sting.

159
00:12:02,920 --> 00:12:05,680
Your face may look young,

160
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:07,760
but you're the oldest
in the whole building.

161
00:12:08,720 --> 00:12:10,000
Enough, Tonhon.

162
00:12:10,080 --> 00:12:12,200
All three of you

163
00:12:12,280 --> 00:12:13,760
are around the same age anyway.

164
00:12:18,920 --> 00:12:20,800
We finally get to formally
introduce ourselves.

165
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:24,600
I'm Ranne.

166
00:12:24,680 --> 00:12:26,000
I'm the main vocalist,

167
00:12:26,680 --> 00:12:27,800
guitarist,

168
00:12:27,880 --> 00:12:29,320
and band leader.

169
00:12:29,920 --> 00:12:31,360
Welcome, newbie.

170
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:37,200
Glad to be joining you guys.

171
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:42,080
From now on, just call me big bro,

172
00:12:42,160 --> 00:12:43,480
Phatee.

173
00:12:44,280 --> 00:12:45,880
So we can get close faster.

174
00:12:49,640 --> 00:12:50,480
Okay.

175
00:12:54,120 --> 00:12:55,040
Why are you guys smiling?

176
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:55,960
Nothing, big bro.

177
00:12:56,040 --> 00:12:58,440
Come on, practice. It's time to practice.

178
00:12:58,520 --> 00:13:00,360
I'm debuting!

179
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:02,480
START LIVESTREAM

180
00:13:02,560 --> 00:13:05,240
Today, we're practicing
some basic dance moves.

181
00:13:07,640 --> 00:13:08,480
Come on.

182
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:10,640
Today, we're practicing the basics.

183
00:13:10,720 --> 00:13:12,520
First move is a bounce. Bend down. Go.

184
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:13,600
1.

185
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:15,360
2.

186
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:17,360
3. That's right.

187
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:18,360
4.

188
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:19,640
5.

189
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:20,920
6.

190
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:21,920
7.

191
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:23,040
8, then back to 1.

192
00:13:23,120 --> 00:13:25,000
1, go. 2.

193
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:26,680
3.

194
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:28,160
4, come on.

195
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:30,080
Now, for the second move,
we'll use our legs.

196
00:13:30,160 --> 00:13:31,840
Start with your feet together.

197
00:13:31,920 --> 00:13:33,800
Step to the right, 1.

198
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:35,640
2.

199
00:13:35,720 --> 00:13:37,240
Bring your right foot in.

200
00:13:37,320 --> 00:13:38,840
Then left foot, go.

201
00:13:39,520 --> 00:13:40,480
Back.

202
00:13:40,560 --> 00:13:42,440
Together. Forward.

203
00:13:43,160 --> 00:13:44,840
Together. Okay, faster now.

204
00:13:44,920 --> 00:13:47,040
5, 6, 7, 8. Go.

205
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:49,120
1, 2, 3,

206
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:51,200
4, 5, 6.

207
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:53,680
Sorry.

208
00:13:56,560 --> 00:13:57,440
Everyone, take a break.

209
00:13:58,240 --> 00:13:59,360
Except you.

210
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:01,360
Keep practicing.

211
00:14:03,120 --> 00:14:04,120
Come on.

212
00:14:06,680 --> 00:14:08,040
Let's work on your footwork. Again.

213
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:09,880
Start. 1.

214
00:14:10,680 --> 00:14:12,280
Right. 2.

215
00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:14,280
Back. Left.

216
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:17,080
Bring your right foot in. 3.

217
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:19,080
Right.

218
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:20,240
Then bend down a little.

219
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:22,400
Then your left foot forward. 4.

220
00:14:23,440 --> 00:14:25,000
Right. Bring this foot in.

221
00:14:25,080 --> 00:14:26,280
Right, cross.

222
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:27,320
5.

223
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:29,360
Bring it in. 6.

224
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,040
Step forward. 7.

225
00:14:31,680 --> 00:14:32,640
Bring your foot in. 8.

226
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:36,480
Can he handle it?

227
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:40,080
It's only his first day.

228
00:14:41,360 --> 00:14:43,280
Shouldn't he have some basics down?

229
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:45,760
You guys were like this
on your first day too.

230
00:14:47,440 --> 00:14:48,440
7.

231
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:50,080
8.

232
00:14:53,480 --> 00:14:54,880
Damn it.

233
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:56,520
I thought we'd finally get to debut.

234
00:14:57,120 --> 00:14:59,000
Now I'm starting to stress out.

235
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:01,520
Damn, I thought
he'd have some basics down.

236
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:03,400
He's clearly below zero.

237
00:15:04,560 --> 00:15:05,960
You guys.

238
00:15:06,040 --> 00:15:07,040
Go back and practice.

239
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:10,920
I just came out for some fresh air.

240
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:12,840
The air inside was so damn stuffy.

241
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:25,000
Don't overthink it.

242
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:27,600
I was way worse on my first day.

243
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:30,920
I really can't dance.

244
00:15:31,480 --> 00:15:32,640
You don't have to comfort me.

245
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:36,080
I'm not comforting you. I'm serious.

246
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:39,120
It took me a long time
to get this good at dancing.

247
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:41,080
It's only your first day.

248
00:15:41,160 --> 00:15:42,240
Don't worry.

249
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:44,440
You can do it.

250
00:15:51,440 --> 00:15:52,440
How about this?

251
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:56,120
I'll help teach you to dance.

252
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:57,240
Okay?

253
00:15:58,720 --> 00:16:00,720
I don't want to trouble you, Ranne.

254
00:16:03,240 --> 00:16:04,960
We're in the same boat now.

255
00:16:05,040 --> 00:16:06,800
We have to help each other
make it to shore.

256
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:09,440
Besides,

257
00:16:09,520 --> 00:16:11,040
I told you to call me big bro.

258
00:16:11,960 --> 00:16:13,400
Don't let me hear you

259
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:14,680
calling me just Ranne again.

260
00:16:14,760 --> 00:16:16,160
It sounds distant.

261
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:26,880
Are you touched?

262
00:16:28,640 --> 00:16:29,640
No.

263
00:16:30,360 --> 00:16:31,720
If I call you big bro,

264
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:33,400
you'll sound too old.

265
00:16:35,240 --> 00:16:36,400
You little brat.

266
00:16:37,760 --> 00:16:39,280
I was being serious.

267
00:16:45,880 --> 00:16:51,160
Do… Re…

268
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:55,160
Mi…

269
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:57,520
Go. 1, 2, 3, 4.

270
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:59,600
5, 6, 7, 8. Go.

271
00:16:59,680 --> 00:17:01,640
2, 2, 3, 4.

272
00:17:01,720 --> 00:17:03,720
5, 6, 7, 8. Go.

273
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:05,480
3, 2, 3, 4.

274
00:17:05,560 --> 00:17:07,720
5, 6, 7, 8.

275
00:17:07,800 --> 00:17:09,720
4, 2, 3, 4.

276
00:17:09,800 --> 00:17:11,400
5, 6, 7, 8.

277
00:17:11,480 --> 00:17:12,520
<i>Feel it here.</i>

278
00:17:13,599 --> 00:17:15,280
Then push it down.

279
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:17,599
Bring it down first.

280
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:19,200
Then bring it out.

281
00:17:20,119 --> 00:17:21,400
Then down again.

282
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:23,800
Go as deep as you can.

283
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:32,800
Come look at this.

284
00:17:32,880 --> 00:17:34,480
How about a lower key?

285
00:17:35,160 --> 00:17:36,640
You mean lower the key?

286
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:38,000
<i>Here, let me show you.</i>

287
00:17:38,080 --> 00:17:40,800
I'll teach you. Here, like this.

288
00:17:41,480 --> 00:17:42,880
Sweep your hand down like this.

289
00:17:42,960 --> 00:17:46,080
Then sweep your hand
past your face like this.

290
00:17:48,280 --> 00:17:49,280
Is this enough?

291
00:17:50,320 --> 00:17:52,080
Yes. Turn your face that way.

292
00:17:58,160 --> 00:17:59,160
Phatee.

293
00:17:59,240 --> 00:18:00,320
Okay.

294
00:18:01,360 --> 00:18:03,920
‪Do…

295
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:08,720
Re…

296
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:12,520
Thanks.

297
00:19:20,600 --> 00:19:21,560
This works.

298
00:19:22,600 --> 00:19:23,600
Oh.

299
00:19:25,040 --> 00:19:28,120
Lately, we've been practicing late
every night.

300
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:30,000
Thanks for putting in the effort.

301
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:33,000
You're doing things you're not good at,

302
00:19:34,080 --> 00:19:36,640
and you have to adjust to
the other members too.

303
00:19:37,720 --> 00:19:40,360
I know the first step is always hard.

304
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:43,080
But I'll stay by your side

305
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:44,680
and keep pushing you forward.

306
00:19:47,120 --> 00:19:49,400
I'm here because of you.

307
00:19:50,320 --> 00:19:52,480
You've always been my inspiration.

308
00:20:00,280 --> 00:20:01,400
Hold on.

309
00:20:04,680 --> 00:20:05,840
Okay.

310
00:20:05,920 --> 00:20:07,640
What you just said was…

311
00:20:08,440 --> 00:20:09,440
for content?

312
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:11,920
Yeah.

313
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:14,200
We have to make content
for the label's channel too.

314
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:16,240
Right now,

315
00:20:16,320 --> 00:20:18,080
we're in the pre-debut phase, right?

316
00:20:18,160 --> 00:20:19,600
It helps attract fans.

317
00:20:20,520 --> 00:20:23,040
Besides, it's the label's promo plan.

318
00:20:23,840 --> 00:20:25,120
Didn't Kao tell you?

319
00:20:28,920 --> 00:20:31,520
Or… did it look fake?
We can do another take.

320
00:20:31,600 --> 00:20:32,800
No.

321
00:20:33,400 --> 00:20:35,040
I think that was…

322
00:20:35,120 --> 00:20:36,280
fine.

323
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:38,440
If we shoot it again, it'll look fake.

324
00:20:42,360 --> 00:20:43,560
Oh, and,

325
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:45,400
you just said

326
00:20:45,480 --> 00:20:47,720
I've always been your inspiration.

327
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:50,160
Did you know me before?

328
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:56,040
I was just saying stuff.

329
00:20:57,280 --> 00:20:58,640
Really?

330
00:20:58,720 --> 00:20:59,680
But you don't seem

331
00:20:59,760 --> 00:21:01,400
like someone who just says stuff.

332
00:21:04,560 --> 00:21:05,720
Well…

333
00:21:07,440 --> 00:21:08,680
it's for content.

334
00:21:09,280 --> 00:21:10,280
I've been practicing.

335
00:21:11,560 --> 00:21:12,720
Very good.

336
00:21:12,800 --> 00:21:13,720
From now on,

337
00:21:13,800 --> 00:21:16,200
the two of us have to
make content together.

338
00:21:17,160 --> 00:21:18,320
So from now on,

339
00:21:19,240 --> 00:21:20,160
when you see a camera,

340
00:21:20,240 --> 00:21:21,560
give it a smile.

341
00:21:21,640 --> 00:21:22,640
Okay?

342
00:21:24,120 --> 00:21:25,120
Okay.

343
00:21:25,640 --> 00:21:26,600
Come on, smile.

344
00:21:28,480 --> 00:21:29,600
Come on, smile.

345
00:21:30,640 --> 00:21:32,040
Come on, smile.

346
00:21:33,440 --> 00:21:34,440
Show your teeth too.

347
00:22:11,240 --> 00:22:12,240
Let's keep eating.

348
00:22:27,520 --> 00:22:28,640
Look at this, guys.

349
00:22:42,640 --> 00:22:44,080
No joke.

350
00:22:44,160 --> 00:22:45,520
I think

351
00:22:45,600 --> 00:22:46,880
since Phatee joined,

352
00:22:46,960 --> 00:22:49,600
our band's engagement has shot way up.

353
00:22:49,680 --> 00:22:51,600
I'm starting to love Phatee.

354
00:22:51,680 --> 00:22:53,400
At first, I saw he couldn't really dance.

355
00:22:53,480 --> 00:22:55,280
Turns out, people really are

356
00:22:55,360 --> 00:22:56,720
good at different things.

357
00:22:56,800 --> 00:22:59,240
Phatee really is talented.

358
00:22:59,320 --> 00:23:01,520
It's not just about pulling in views.

359
00:23:01,600 --> 00:23:02,640
Look over there.

360
00:23:08,080 --> 00:23:09,000
Take a look.

361
00:23:14,920 --> 00:23:16,360
He's even better than me.

362
00:23:18,840 --> 00:23:21,160
Let's cut the rap. It's too much.
It won't have that wow factor.

363
00:23:22,320 --> 00:23:23,360
Let's do it.

364
00:23:23,440 --> 00:23:26,040
Something like this. Take a look.

365
00:23:28,080 --> 00:23:29,320
Whoa.

366
00:23:29,400 --> 00:23:30,320
It's really good.

367
00:23:30,400 --> 00:23:31,800
Hey, everyone.

368
00:23:31,880 --> 00:23:32,800
Phatee's old song,

369
00:23:32,880 --> 00:23:34,440
with a new arrangement,

370
00:23:34,520 --> 00:23:36,000
is finished!

371
00:23:36,080 --> 00:23:37,520
- Come here.
- Let me see.

372
00:23:37,600 --> 00:23:38,680
Come check it out.

373
00:23:40,320 --> 00:23:41,560
Let's see.

374
00:23:41,640 --> 00:23:42,720
Check this out.

375
00:23:47,080 --> 00:23:49,160
- Whoa.
- Shit!

376
00:23:50,320 --> 00:23:51,760
He can compose this well?

377
00:23:51,840 --> 00:23:53,440
This is the real deal.

378
00:23:53,520 --> 00:23:55,040
It's not that hard.

379
00:23:55,120 --> 00:23:57,080
Hey, you could be a little humble.

380
00:23:59,320 --> 00:24:01,960
How about we

381
00:24:02,040 --> 00:24:03,160
try playing it?

382
00:24:03,800 --> 00:24:05,080
- Let's do it.
- Let's try it.

383
00:24:05,160 --> 00:24:07,000
- We're trying it now?
- Yeah, let's try it now.

384
00:24:07,080 --> 00:24:09,160
- Hey, what are you afraid of?
- We won't know until we try.

385
00:24:09,240 --> 00:24:10,440
Okay, come on.

386
00:24:10,520 --> 00:24:12,240
- Do you remember the chords?
- I do.

387
00:24:12,320 --> 00:24:13,160
Let's do it.

388
00:25:44,480 --> 00:25:45,640
Whose song is this?

389
00:25:49,560 --> 00:25:50,640
Well…

390
00:25:50,720 --> 00:25:52,920
It's an old song of Phatee's

391
00:25:53,000 --> 00:25:54,560
that we rearranged.

392
00:26:02,560 --> 00:26:05,640
Okay. Good.
Let's make this your debut song.

393
00:26:06,720 --> 00:26:07,720
Really?

394
00:26:07,800 --> 00:26:09,080
Really.

395
00:26:09,160 --> 00:26:10,640
It's your time now.

396
00:26:10,720 --> 00:26:12,880
You can start recording the song,

397
00:26:12,960 --> 00:26:15,280
planning the promotion,
and shooting the MV.

398
00:26:15,360 --> 00:26:17,320
You don't have to wait
three months anymore.

399
00:26:17,400 --> 00:26:18,720
If you're ready, just debut.

400
00:26:21,400 --> 00:26:22,680
We're finally debuting!

401
00:26:22,760 --> 00:26:24,760
We did it!

402
00:26:25,560 --> 00:26:27,240
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

403
00:26:30,160 --> 00:26:34,560
Thanks, Phatee. It's all because of you
that our band has come this far.

404
00:26:35,360 --> 00:26:37,160
It's not that big a deal.

405
00:26:39,360 --> 00:26:40,640
Come on, be happy.

406
00:26:40,720 --> 00:26:42,160
Come on, after everything you've done.

407
00:26:44,440 --> 00:26:47,240
We did it!

408
00:27:01,680 --> 00:27:03,120
Why are you back so early today?

409
00:27:06,280 --> 00:27:08,440
It's already 2 a.m.

410
00:27:09,960 --> 00:27:11,920
You usually get back at 3 or 4 a.m.

411
00:27:12,680 --> 00:27:14,840
So? Is being a trainee fun?

412
00:27:16,560 --> 00:27:17,680
It's not bad.

413
00:27:26,600 --> 00:27:27,920
If you want to talk, go ahead.

414
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:30,320
If not, have a drink with me.

415
00:27:41,760 --> 00:27:43,640
I've seen your clips
all over social media.

416
00:27:43,720 --> 00:27:45,120
You're getting a lot of buzz.

417
00:27:45,200 --> 00:27:47,720
People are even shipping you with Ranne.

418
00:27:48,920 --> 00:27:50,680
He's the one who kept
pursuing you at the club, right?

419
00:27:53,040 --> 00:27:54,240
It's just content.

420
00:27:55,480 --> 00:27:57,920
Why? You don't like it?

421
00:27:59,320 --> 00:28:00,840
I don't know either.

422
00:28:00,920 --> 00:28:02,280
I don't know if

423
00:28:02,360 --> 00:28:04,200
Ranne is nice to me

424
00:28:04,280 --> 00:28:06,320
because he genuinely wants to be,

425
00:28:07,360 --> 00:28:08,360
or because…

426
00:28:09,560 --> 00:28:10,960
we just have to work together.

427
00:28:12,920 --> 00:28:14,480
I thought it was something serious.

428
00:28:15,240 --> 00:28:16,560
So it's a matter of the heart.

429
00:28:19,560 --> 00:28:20,960
What would you do?

430
00:28:21,840 --> 00:28:23,200
I wouldn't care

431
00:28:23,280 --> 00:28:25,120
whether he's doing it for work

432
00:28:25,200 --> 00:28:26,720
or because of personal feelings.

433
00:28:27,760 --> 00:28:29,560
I'd make the most of it.

434
00:28:30,160 --> 00:28:31,720
It's like dreaming.

435
00:28:31,800 --> 00:28:33,560
You know you'll have to wake up,

436
00:28:33,640 --> 00:28:35,080
but so what?

437
00:28:35,160 --> 00:28:36,680
Just dreaming makes you happy, right?

438
00:28:37,360 --> 00:28:39,120
What if I wake up from the dream?

439
00:28:39,640 --> 00:28:41,080
Then you have two choices.

440
00:28:41,160 --> 00:28:42,880
Go back to sleep

441
00:28:43,400 --> 00:28:45,320
and hope you have
the same good dream again.

442
00:28:45,400 --> 00:28:46,800
Or

443
00:28:46,880 --> 00:28:49,080
make your dream a reality.

444
00:29:11,360 --> 00:29:12,840
Scrub harder.

445
00:29:12,920 --> 00:29:14,120
Do you have any strength?

446
00:29:19,920 --> 00:29:20,840
Like this.

447
00:29:21,920 --> 00:29:22,880
Like this.

448
00:29:24,600 --> 00:29:26,880
You're still as strong as ever.

449
00:29:28,400 --> 00:29:30,320
You should eat more.

450
00:29:30,400 --> 00:29:31,920
You're so skinny.

451
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:33,920
One puff and you'd blow away.

452
00:29:38,360 --> 00:29:39,520
Oh.

453
00:29:39,600 --> 00:29:41,880
You're Tangmo's ex.

454
00:29:41,960 --> 00:29:43,320
You're at The Crow Club now?

455
00:29:44,240 --> 00:29:45,520
Or did you two get back together?

456
00:29:45,600 --> 00:29:48,680
Stop it, Vann. Want a smack?

457
00:29:48,760 --> 00:29:49,760
I just…

458
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:52,880
hired him to clean.

459
00:29:52,960 --> 00:29:54,880
I'm lazy.

460
00:29:54,960 --> 00:29:55,920
That's all.

461
00:29:57,560 --> 00:30:00,040
But it looks like you're the one cleaning.

462
00:30:03,400 --> 00:30:05,920
Keep scrubbing. Make sure it's clean.

463
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:07,720
Then go scrub the bathroom too.

464
00:30:13,480 --> 00:30:14,720
Don't panic.

465
00:30:15,880 --> 00:30:17,760
The more you panic,
the more suspicious you look.

466
00:30:18,760 --> 00:30:20,080
Even if there's nothing,

467
00:30:21,040 --> 00:30:23,000
people will think there is.

468
00:30:57,000 --> 00:30:58,160
What's this?

469
00:30:59,480 --> 00:31:00,880
It's your debut song.

470
00:31:01,600 --> 00:31:03,080
What did you do to it?

471
00:31:03,160 --> 00:31:04,600
The original was already good.

472
00:31:05,320 --> 00:31:08,480
I tried having AI polish it.
I didn't do anything.

473
00:31:09,320 --> 00:31:10,720
You used AI?

474
00:31:10,800 --> 00:31:11,880
Saw.

475
00:31:13,200 --> 00:31:15,200
There are plenty of producers
at your label.

476
00:31:15,280 --> 00:31:16,720
I can do it too.

477
00:31:16,800 --> 00:31:18,680
I didn't use AI for everything.

478
00:31:18,760 --> 00:31:20,040
Just to polish it up.

479
00:31:20,120 --> 00:31:21,680
What the fuck do you mean you didn't?

480
00:31:21,760 --> 00:31:23,520
You changed almost the whole song.

481
00:31:23,600 --> 00:31:25,680
What's the point of art if you do this?

482
00:31:25,760 --> 00:31:27,040
So what do you want?

483
00:31:27,120 --> 00:31:28,840
If you're debuting with this song,

484
00:31:28,920 --> 00:31:30,240
then they can debut as four.

485
00:31:30,320 --> 00:31:31,680
- I'm out.
- Hey.

486
00:31:31,760 --> 00:31:32,800
Saw.

487
00:31:32,880 --> 00:31:34,000
Don't say that, Saw.

488
00:31:34,080 --> 00:31:36,080
If the label owner wants to use AI,

489
00:31:36,160 --> 00:31:38,560
why not use AI to create an artist?

490
00:31:38,640 --> 00:31:40,280
That seems more your style.

491
00:31:41,320 --> 00:31:43,440
- Saw.
- Saw.

492
00:31:43,520 --> 00:31:44,800
- Fuck.
- What's his problem?

493
00:31:44,880 --> 00:31:47,080
He's making such a big deal out of this.

494
00:31:47,160 --> 00:31:49,120
But I think this band will make it anyway

495
00:31:49,200 --> 00:31:51,280
with Phatee and Ranne.

496
00:31:51,360 --> 00:31:55,040
They're both getting
a lot of buzz right now.

497
00:31:55,920 --> 00:31:57,520
What do you guys think?

498
00:31:57,600 --> 00:31:59,360
If you continue without Saw?

499
00:32:00,480 --> 00:32:02,080
If we had a choice,

500
00:32:02,160 --> 00:32:03,840
we'd rather debut as five.

501
00:32:04,520 --> 00:32:07,480
Then I'll give you three days.

502
00:32:07,560 --> 00:32:09,280
Think it over.

503
00:32:09,360 --> 00:32:11,160
If Saw doesn't come back,

504
00:32:11,240 --> 00:32:12,520
what are you going to do?

505
00:32:30,160 --> 00:32:31,280
What the hell?

506
00:32:58,440 --> 00:33:00,680
You could call him
a hundred times. He won't answer.

507
00:33:00,760 --> 00:33:02,440
When he's ready, he'll come talk to you.

508
00:33:04,160 --> 00:33:05,400
So what are you going to do

509
00:33:05,480 --> 00:33:06,880
if he quits?

510
00:33:07,520 --> 00:33:09,600
Everything's been set for five people,

511
00:33:09,680 --> 00:33:11,800
both the blocking and vocal parts.

512
00:33:11,880 --> 00:33:13,480
I'm not giving up that easily.

513
00:33:14,400 --> 00:33:15,880
You guys go home for today.

514
00:33:16,800 --> 00:33:18,160
I'll handle Saw myself.

515
00:33:20,200 --> 00:33:21,440
Keep us posted.

516
00:33:38,240 --> 00:33:41,120
Why haven't you left yet?

517
00:33:42,680 --> 00:33:43,880
You looked stressed,

518
00:33:44,760 --> 00:33:46,040
so I'm staying with you.

519
00:33:49,640 --> 00:33:51,200
Let's call it a day.

520
00:33:51,720 --> 00:33:52,920
I'll take you home.

521
00:33:54,160 --> 00:33:56,520
Isn't it
in the opposite direction for you?

522
00:33:59,160 --> 00:34:00,160
It's fine.

523
00:34:00,880 --> 00:34:02,800
I was going to see Saw too.

524
00:34:04,160 --> 00:34:05,720
Then I'll come with you.

525
00:34:17,239 --> 00:34:19,199
Can you open it for me?

526
00:34:29,840 --> 00:34:32,600
Saw must've known I was coming.

527
00:34:32,679 --> 00:34:34,280
That's why he hasn't come back.

528
00:34:34,360 --> 00:34:36,239
He's not posting on social media.

529
00:34:37,040 --> 00:34:38,400
He won't reply to my texts either.

530
00:34:42,120 --> 00:34:43,840
You probably need to give him some time.

531
00:34:43,920 --> 00:34:45,920
Where on earth is he?

532
00:34:46,840 --> 00:34:48,440
He doesn't have many friends.

533
00:34:51,199 --> 00:34:52,840
Or…

534
00:34:52,920 --> 00:34:54,840
maybe he went back to his parents.

535
00:34:55,440 --> 00:34:57,520
Or he's staying with
a sibling for a while.

536
00:34:59,920 --> 00:35:01,120
Right.

537
00:35:01,200 --> 00:35:02,880
Saw has an older sister.

538
00:35:03,840 --> 00:35:06,120
But I messaged her,
and she hasn't replied yet.

539
00:35:07,280 --> 00:35:09,920
I don't know
where his parents live either.

540
00:35:10,920 --> 00:35:12,440
But he could be there.

541
00:35:14,480 --> 00:35:17,080
Then wait for his sister to reply first.

542
00:35:17,160 --> 00:35:19,160
Then figure out what to do.

543
00:35:23,120 --> 00:35:24,120
You know,

544
00:35:25,960 --> 00:35:28,520
we've given up on
this dream so many times.

545
00:35:30,440 --> 00:35:31,760
We're so close.

546
00:35:32,960 --> 00:35:34,360
We're really so close.

547
00:35:36,200 --> 00:35:38,080
We have to debut as five.

548
00:36:04,200 --> 00:36:05,720
Thanks.

549
00:36:09,520 --> 00:36:11,160
Aren't you practicing with the band today?

550
00:36:12,120 --> 00:36:13,480
Not today.

551
00:36:16,960 --> 00:36:19,080
Have you ever taken a job finding someone?

552
00:36:19,160 --> 00:36:20,800
Not often.

553
00:36:20,880 --> 00:36:23,200
Linda usually gives
jobs like that to Mimi.

554
00:36:24,080 --> 00:36:27,200
She's an expert at catching cheaters
and finding missing people.

555
00:36:27,280 --> 00:36:29,280
Missing dogs and cats too.
That's her specialty.

556
00:36:30,160 --> 00:36:31,080
Why?

557
00:36:31,600 --> 00:36:33,840
Someone in my band
had a fight with the label,

558
00:36:33,920 --> 00:36:35,120
and then he disappeared.

559
00:36:36,440 --> 00:36:37,720
What's that got to do with you?

560
00:36:39,200 --> 00:36:40,320
Well…

561
00:36:40,400 --> 00:36:43,360
it has nothing to do with me.
But it has to do with Ranne.

562
00:36:47,000 --> 00:36:48,400
Heart trouble again.

563
00:36:52,640 --> 00:36:53,560
Yeah.

564
00:36:55,880 --> 00:36:57,560
Is Mimi here?

565
00:36:58,400 --> 00:36:59,960
Mimi's not here.

566
00:37:08,000 --> 00:37:08,960
Let me see.

567
00:37:09,040 --> 00:37:11,440
Who are you looking for?

568
00:37:18,520 --> 00:37:19,920
His name is Saw.

569
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:22,800
He might be hard to find
because he rarely posts anything.

570
00:37:23,400 --> 00:37:24,760
Saw.

571
00:37:33,160 --> 00:37:34,880
Do you believe in fate?

572
00:37:36,760 --> 00:37:37,760
What's with you?

573
00:37:37,840 --> 00:37:39,800
Are you picking someone
based on a profile picture?

574
00:37:40,720 --> 00:37:42,040
No!

575
00:37:42,560 --> 00:37:44,600
Linda just told me about a job
where I'd pretend

576
00:37:44,680 --> 00:37:46,880
to be someone's boyfriend
to fool her family.

577
00:37:46,960 --> 00:37:49,000
And the person who contacted us…

578
00:37:50,480 --> 00:37:51,520
is this girl.

579
00:37:53,480 --> 00:37:54,440
When?

580
00:37:55,120 --> 00:37:56,200
This afternoon.

581
00:38:11,280 --> 00:38:14,120
With you two staring like that,
my boyfriend's getting nervous.

582
00:38:15,560 --> 00:38:17,480
Your name is Sky, right?

583
00:38:18,440 --> 00:38:19,360
Yes.

584
00:38:19,440 --> 00:38:21,240
What do you do?

585
00:38:23,960 --> 00:38:26,080
I'm an engineer.

586
00:38:26,160 --> 00:38:27,200
I work for a construction company.

587
00:38:28,920 --> 00:38:30,600
Good career.

588
00:38:30,680 --> 00:38:31,840
Good-looking too.

589
00:38:31,920 --> 00:38:33,560
I like this one.

590
00:38:33,640 --> 00:38:35,640
I don't want another one like your ex.

591
00:38:35,720 --> 00:38:36,920
I know.

592
00:38:37,520 --> 00:38:39,480
Where do you live?

593
00:38:41,080 --> 00:38:42,360
I live in Lat Phrao.

594
00:38:42,440 --> 00:38:44,200
Is it a condo or a townhouse?

595
00:38:45,520 --> 00:38:46,680
- Mom.
- It's a condo.

596
00:38:46,760 --> 00:38:48,760
How did you get here?
What car did you drive?

597
00:38:48,840 --> 00:38:50,000
Dad.

598
00:38:50,600 --> 00:38:51,520
I took a Grab.

599
00:38:51,600 --> 00:38:53,800
Oh, so you don't have
to worry about parking.

600
00:38:55,680 --> 00:38:57,120
There he is.

601
00:39:00,720 --> 00:39:02,360
How did you get here?

602
00:39:07,600 --> 00:39:10,520
You know your sister's boyfriend too?

603
00:39:10,600 --> 00:39:11,840
Boyfriend?

604
00:39:13,400 --> 00:39:14,520
Yes.

605
00:39:14,600 --> 00:39:16,480
This is Sky, my boyfriend.

606
00:39:16,560 --> 00:39:18,280
How would you know my boyfriend?

607
00:39:23,680 --> 00:39:25,640
Maybe I mistook him for someone else.

608
00:39:26,680 --> 00:39:27,840
Okay, okay.

609
00:39:27,920 --> 00:39:29,800
Come on, let's eat.

610
00:39:29,880 --> 00:39:31,560
You must all be starving.

611
00:39:33,240 --> 00:39:36,120
- Eat a lot so you'll grow.
- Okay.

612
00:39:51,080 --> 00:39:52,200
Ranne.

613
00:39:52,800 --> 00:39:55,640
Ranne, can I take a photo with you?

614
00:39:55,720 --> 00:39:56,840
Sure.

615
00:40:00,800 --> 00:40:02,400
Thank you.

616
00:40:12,320 --> 00:40:13,600
Excuse me.

617
00:40:13,680 --> 00:40:15,040
Is Phatee here?

618
00:40:15,120 --> 00:40:17,040
I haven't been able to reach him all day.

619
00:40:17,120 --> 00:40:18,240
I was wondering who it was.

620
00:40:18,320 --> 00:40:19,640
It's Phatee's ship partner.

621
00:40:19,720 --> 00:40:21,880
Phatee's not here. He's working.

622
00:40:21,960 --> 00:40:23,480
But he'll be back soon.

623
00:40:24,040 --> 00:40:26,360
Then I'll wait here.

624
00:40:29,680 --> 00:40:32,040
I don't think it's good to stay here.
There's no privacy.

625
00:40:32,120 --> 00:40:34,120
Want to go to Phatee's room?
I'll take you.

626
00:40:35,720 --> 00:40:38,520
- Okay. Sorry to trouble you.
- He's so handsome.

627
00:40:38,600 --> 00:40:40,400
We have to tell our friends.

628
00:40:40,480 --> 00:40:42,520
Post it in the group.

629
00:40:44,240 --> 00:40:46,680
- I'll share it with my friends on IG.
- Drinks are here.

630
00:40:47,200 --> 00:40:48,040
Thanks.

631
00:40:55,360 --> 00:40:57,080
That scared me.

632
00:41:02,960 --> 00:41:04,560
I haven't seen you for a while,

633
00:41:04,640 --> 00:41:05,680
and you already changed your name.

634
00:41:08,640 --> 00:41:10,480
And now you're my sister's boyfriend.

635
00:41:12,520 --> 00:41:14,000
If I didn't do this,

636
00:41:14,840 --> 00:41:16,240
would I get to see you?

637
00:41:18,160 --> 00:41:20,360
Ranne and everyone
are really worried about you.

638
00:41:21,800 --> 00:41:23,520
Are you really leaving
the band this easily?

639
00:41:27,200 --> 00:41:28,960
Would you dare sing that AI song?

640
00:41:30,640 --> 00:41:32,440
Just go talk to Kao.

641
00:41:37,520 --> 00:41:38,880
Kao won't listen to me.

642
00:41:40,600 --> 00:41:41,960
She doesn't care about anyone

643
00:41:43,240 --> 00:41:44,600
except you and Ranne.

644
00:41:47,080 --> 00:41:48,280
What's with you?

645
00:41:51,320 --> 00:41:52,680
You really don't know?

646
00:41:53,720 --> 00:41:55,280
You only get to debut

647
00:41:56,320 --> 00:41:58,120
because they're selling
your ship with Ranne.

648
00:42:04,040 --> 00:42:05,560
How do you know?

649
00:42:06,920 --> 00:42:08,480
It might not be that serious.

650
00:42:09,360 --> 00:42:10,960
How could I not know?

651
00:42:12,680 --> 00:42:14,640
Ranne just didn't want me to tell you.

652
00:42:14,720 --> 00:42:15,760
And now,

653
00:42:16,520 --> 00:42:19,040
you and Ranne
are getting lots of jobs together.

654
00:42:20,440 --> 00:42:23,160
But Ranne told Kao
he wants to take them after debut.

655
00:42:24,600 --> 00:42:25,960
Otherwise, you'd feel pressured

656
00:42:27,000 --> 00:42:28,600
and turn down the jobs.

657
00:42:31,120 --> 00:42:32,600
That's why Kao wants you to debut soon.

658
00:42:37,080 --> 00:42:38,360
But I went along with it

659
00:42:40,480 --> 00:42:43,040
because at least
I'd get closer to my dream.

660
00:42:45,800 --> 00:42:47,640
But now I guess Kao doesn't
even see me anymore.

661
00:42:49,040 --> 00:42:50,880
So I don't know why I should stay.

662
00:42:56,560 --> 00:42:58,800
What if I get them to stop using AI

663
00:43:00,120 --> 00:43:01,520
and use the song you wrote?

664
00:43:03,160 --> 00:43:04,200
Will you come back?

665
00:43:07,600 --> 00:43:08,880
Without me,

666
00:43:09,800 --> 00:43:11,080
you can still debut.

667
00:43:12,760 --> 00:43:13,800
I'm not important.

668
00:43:15,640 --> 00:43:16,920
That's not true.

669
00:43:17,960 --> 00:43:19,080
You are important.

670
00:44:20,280 --> 00:44:22,640
SONGBOOK

671
00:45:02,080 --> 00:45:03,560
RANNE

672
00:45:05,520 --> 00:45:08,000
<i>- I'm putting mine here.</i>
<i>- I'll stick mine here.</i>

673
00:45:08,080 --> 00:45:09,600
I really like you.

674
00:45:09,680 --> 00:45:12,760
- Thank you.
- Ranne, I'm putting mine here.

675
00:45:13,360 --> 00:45:15,640
Happy Valentine's Day.

676
00:45:16,680 --> 00:45:18,520
There's Phatee. Come on.

677
00:45:18,600 --> 00:45:20,960
- Phatee!
- Phatee!

678
00:45:27,040 --> 00:45:28,640
I really like you.

679
00:45:30,240 --> 00:45:33,640
RANNE

680
00:46:24,400 --> 00:46:25,800
So what's going on with you and Phatee?

681
00:46:25,880 --> 00:46:28,880
<i>The way he looks at you is nothing</i>
<i>like how he looks at anyone else.</i>

682
00:46:28,960 --> 00:46:31,880
- Do you like me?
<i>- The opportunity is here.</i>

683
00:46:31,960 --> 00:46:32,840
You have to seize it.

684
00:46:32,920 --> 00:46:34,480
Which one do you mean?

685
00:46:34,560 --> 00:46:36,480
<i>Both your dream and your love life.</i>

686
00:46:36,560 --> 00:46:38,200
Come on, let's go see Phatee.

687
00:46:38,280 --> 00:46:40,320
Why did you bring me here? It's crowded.

688
00:46:40,400 --> 00:46:41,920
Then just keep looking at me like this.

689
00:46:42,000 --> 00:46:43,960
Did you trick me into looking at you?

690
00:46:44,040 --> 00:46:48,240
<i>Close your eyes and think about</i>
<i>what you want to happen.</i>

691
00:46:48,320 --> 00:46:49,320
<i>You can open your eyes now.</i>
